0,Purubora language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purubora_language,"August 30, 2025 - The Puruborá language of Brazil is one of the Tupian languages. It is also known as Aurã, Cujubim, Burubora, Kuyubi, Migueleno, Miguelenho or Pumbora. Specifically, it is spoken in the Brazilian state of Rondônia, in Costa Marques and around the headwaters of the Rio São Miguel tributary ...",Puruborá,Tupian
